<title>INDIA: Indian metals mixed on world setback news.</title>
<headline>Indian metals mixed on world setback news.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian nickel prices weakened while other metals were unchanged on Thursday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Ready nickel fell by 100 rupees to 39,200 rupees per quintal on profit-taking following reports of a world market setback.</p>
<p>Copper was unchanged at 11,850 rupees, as was the case in zinc (6,325 rupees) and lead (5,000 rupees), dealers said.</p>
<p>Tin was quoted at 35,900 rupees and aluminium at 7,450.</p>
<p>-- Bombay Commodities +91-22-265 9000</p>
